From: Octagon SF8008 port
Subject: [PATCH] gfbdc: do not swap in an unallocated back surface

The CONFIG_HISILICON_FB block at the end of setResolution() swaps
surface and surface_back unconditionally. When the framebuffer only
provides a single page, setResolution() has just set surface_back.data
and surface_back.data_phys to 0, so the swap installs a NULL pointer as
the live drawing surface and the next gPixmap::fill() dereferences
address 0.

Only perform the swap when the back surface actually has memory.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
+++ b/lib/gdi/gfbdc.cpp
@@ -523,7 +523,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_HISILICON_FB)
-	if(islocked()==0)
+	if(islocked()==0 && surface_back.data)
 	{
 		gUnmanagedSurface s(surface);
 		surface = surface_back;
